### 19. PERFORMANCE AND FAILURE HANDLING

- Keep factor lookup, unit conversion, and carbon calculations deterministic.
- Avoid expensive full-project recalculations when only one relevant value changes.
- Validate quantities and factors before calculation.
- Handle missing values, invalid units, incompatible modules, and overflow.
- Guard against duplicate requests or stale asynchronous responses.
- Provide clear loading, empty, partial-data, unavailable, warning, and failure states.
- Prevent unbounded scenario expansion or oversized imports from freezing the UI.
- Do not turn failed source lookups into fabricated default factors.
- Do not silently substitute one emission factor for another.
- Clearly distinguish a calculation failure from a result of zero emissions.

